<figure id="S3.T2" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table"><span id="S3.T2.6" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Table 2</span>: </span><span id="S3.T2.7" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:90%;">Performance comparison on VSI-Bench.<span id="S3.T2.7.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium">
We compare <span id="S3.T2.7.1.1" class="ltx_text"><span id="S3.T2.7.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">PyVision</span> </span>-Video with Video-R1, a video understanding model using pure textual reasoning, and VITAL, an agentic video model with predefined video clipping tools.
All methods are based on Qwen2.5-VL-7B and trained with RL.
<span id="S3.T2.7.1.2" class="ltx_text"><span id="S3.T2.7.1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">PyVision</span> </span>-Video achieves a 7.3% absolute improvement over the Qwen2.5-VL-7B baseline, demonstrating the effectiveness of dynamic tooling for spatial reasoning.</span></span></figcaption>
